cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Novomodelo, please cite the version you used. Novomodelo is a
  fork of Cobre; when your work discusses its origin, the architecture or
  methodology it inherits, or results obtained with Cobre itself, please also
  cite Cobre at the version listed under "references".
type: software
title: "Novomodelo"
abstract: >-
  Rust ecosystem for power system optimization: a distributed SDDP solver for
  hydrothermal dispatch, with a CLI and Python bindings. A fork of Cobre
  v0.18.0.
authors:
  - name: "Operador Nacional do Sistema Elétrico - ONS"
    country: BR
    website: "https://www.ons.org.br"
  - name: "Câmara de Comercialização de Energia Elétrica - CCEE"
    country: BR
    website: "https://www.ccee.org.br"
  - name: "Empresa de Pesquisa Energética - EPE"
    country: BR
    website: "https://www.epe.gov.br"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ons-ccee-epe/novomodelo"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - SDDP
  - hydrothermal dispatch
  - stochastic optimization
  - power systems
  - Rust
# No `version` / `date-released`: they would go stale between releases.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Cobre: Open Infrastructure for Power System Computation"
    authors:
      - family-names: Alves
        given-names: "Rogerio J. M."
    version: "0.18.0"
    date-released: 2026-10-07
    commit: "3ab1f748814a87ffd08585096ca9cbe810320cb6"
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23202162
    repository-code: "https://github.com/cobre-rs/cobre"
    license: Apache-2.0
    scope: "The fork point: Novomodelo is a fork of this Cobre release."
    notes: >-
      The name "Cobre" is used here only to describe the origin of the work
      (Apache License 2.0, Section 6).
